    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change keeps all customerCode-building logic in its single owning unit (`AssignOwnerCustomerCode`), and the new CITY3 extraction mirrors the existing LAST3 extraction line-for-line, so the added logic reads as a natural extension rather than a new concern grafted on.\n\n`AssignOwnerMembershipNumber` correctly required no code change \u2014 it derives purely from `customerCode` via string concatenation, so the new format flows through automatically. Updating only its javadoc example (`SYD-SMI-0007-M26`) is exactly the right, minimal touch; adding format logic there would have duplicated responsibility.\n\nThe OpenAPI description and both examples were updated in lockstep with the code, keeping the contract documentation coherent with behavior.\n\nMinor nit (not blocking): `long inCity` immediately followed by `long sequence = inCity + 1` could be a single expression, but it mirrors the original two-line `sequence` shape and keeps the stream count readable, so it's a reasonable stylistic choice consistent with the prior version.",
